# What the knowledge graph is allowed to call "this codebase".
#
# The graph answers architecture questions, so it has to cover the library and
# nothing that merely sits in the same folder. Without this file the rebuild
# sweeps in whatever happens to be on disk, and a reader then cannot tell a
# module from a build product.

# Investigations, not library code. Nothing in src/ imports from here -- see
# development/README.md -- so a call graph that mixes the two invents edges
# that do not exist.
development/

# The built documentation site: minified vendor JavaScript, about six hundred
# nodes of lunr search stemmers. It was in the graph and should not have been.
site/

# An unpacked source distribution: a second copy of the package, which would
# double every symbol in it.
pymicroglia-0.1.0/
